{
  "working": "Thermodynamic system classification: open system exchanges both mass and energy with surroundings; closed system exchanges only energy (no mass); isolated system exchanges neither. Evaluate each statement:\n(A) Hot drink in a perfectly insulated, sealed flask: sealed prevents mass exchange; insulated prevents energy exchange (no heat transfer). Thus it is an isolated system, not open. Statement claims open → incorrect.\n(B) Water boiling in an open beaker: mass (vapor) leaves, energy (heat) can leave; open → correct.\n(C) Gas heated in a sealed rigid steel cylinder: sealed prevents mass exchange; energy can be added via heat (or work), so closed → correct.\n(D) Living cell exchanges matter (nutrients, waste) and energy (heat, metabolic heat); open → correct.\nThus the statement that is NOT correct is (A).",
  "answer": "[TYPE: thermodynamics] [CALC_VALUE: A] [CALC_UNIT: none] [SUBSTANCE: null]",
  "objection": null
}

{
  "working": "An isolated system has no exchange of energy or matter with surroundings. A hot drink in a perfectly insulated, sealed flask cannot exchange heat or matter, so it is isolated. Water boiling in an open beaker exchanges heat and vapor (matter) with surroundings, so not isolated. A living cell exchanges both energy and matter, so not isolated. A gas heated in a sealed rigid cylinder exchanges heat with surroundings (if not insulated) but no mass; thus it is a closed system, not open. Therefore only statement (A) is correct.",
  "answer": "[TYPE: thermodynamics] [CALC_VALUE: A] [CALC_UNIT: none] [SUBSTANCE: null]",
  "objection": null
}

{
  "working": "A closed thermodynamic system exchanges energy but not matter with surroundings. An open system exchanges both. Evaluate each option:\n(A) A living cell exchanges matter (e.g., gases, nutrients) with surroundings → not closed.\n(B) Gas in a sealed rigid steel cylinder: no matter can cross the cylinder wall (closed), energy can be added by heating → closed system.\n(C) Water boiling in an open beaker: vapor leaves as matter → open system, not closed.\n(D) Hot drink in a perfectly insulated, sealed flask: sealed prevents matter exchange; insulation prevents energy exchange (or at least no net energy flow), so closed.\nThus correct statements are (B) and (D).",
  "answer": "[TYPE: thermodynamics] [CALC_VALUE: BD] [CALC_UNIT: none] [SUBSTANCE: null]",
